ground-color:rgba(232,232,232, 0.8);padding:2px;}#mermaid-1784573128661 .icon-shape rect,#mermaid-1784573128661 .image-shape rect{opacity:0.5;background-color:rgba(232,232,232, 0.8);fill:rgba(232,232,232, 0.8);}#mermaid-1784573128661 :root{--mermaid-font-family:"trebuchet ms",verdana,arial,sans-serif;} Exactly 1 Multiple (tie) 0 Yes No Found Not found uri: file:///workspace/foo/src/Main.scala router.route(uri) Phase 1: RoutingTable (longest-prefix via source dirs) reverseLookupCandidates(uri) Matches found? Return connId tieBreakByNearestBspRoot Phase 2: Bootstrap Heuristic Nearest .bsp/ root resolves tie? Return connId Return alphabetically first connId Walk up directory tree Each ancestor has .bsp/? Cache result per directory Return connId Cache as None, return None Phase 1: RoutingTable (Ground Truth) Each connection registers its source directories (from buildTarget/sources BSP response) via registerGroundTruth. The RoutingTable does: // For each URI, find all matching (dirLength, connId) pairs
// Return connIds with the longest matching prefix
def reverseLookupCandidates(uri: String): List[BspConnectionId] = synchronized {
    val matches = entries.toList.flatMap { (connId, dirs) =>
      dirs.collect { case dir if uri.startsWith(dir) => (dir.length, connId) }
    }
    matches.maxByOption(_._1) match
      case Some((bestLen, _)) =>
        matches.collect { case (`bestLen`, connId) => connId }.distinct
      case None => Nil
}
 Example: connection A owns file:///workspace/foo/, connection B owns file:///workspace/foo/bar/. URI file:///workspace/foo/bar/baz.scala routes to B (longer prefix wins). Phase 2: Bootstrap Heuristic (Fallback) When no source directories match, BspRouter walks up from the file's parent directory, checking each ancestor for a .bsp/ subdirectory registered via registerBspRoot. Results are cached per directory so subsequent lookups in the same tree skip the walk. Compile Target Selection Inside BspConnectionSupervisor, selectCompileTargetIds determines which build targets to compile. Three strategies in order: #mermaid-1784573128798{font-family:"trebuchet ms",verdana,arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;fill:#333;}@keyframes edge-animation-frame{from{stroke-dashoffset:0;}}@keyframes dash{to{stroke-dashoffset:0;}}#mermaid-1784573128798 .edge-animation-slow{stroke-dasharray:9,5!important;stroke-dashoffset:900;animation:dash 50s linear infinite;stroke-linecap:round;}#mermaid-1784573128798 .edge-animation-fast{stroke-dasharray:9,5!important;stroke-dashoffset:900;animation:dash 20s linear infinite;stroke-linecap:round;}#mermaid-1784573128798 .error-icon{fill:#552222;}#mermaid-1784573128798 .error-text{fill:#552222;stroke:#552222;}#mermaid-1784573128798 .edge-thickness-normal{stroke-width:1px;}#mermaid-1784573128798 .edge-thickness-thick{stroke-width:3.5px;}#mermaid-1784573128798 .edge-pattern-solid{stroke-dasharray:0;}#mermaid-1784573128798 .edge-thickness-invisible{stroke-width:0;fill:none;}#mermaid-1784573128798 .edge-pattern-dashed{stroke-dasharray:3;}#mermaid-1784573128798 .edge-pattern-dotted{stroke-dasharray:2;}#mermaid-1784573128798 .marker{fill:#333333;stroke:#333333;}#mermaid-1784573128798 .marker.cross{stroke:#333333;}#mermaid-1784573128798 svg{font-family:"trebuchet ms",verdana,arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;}#mermaid-1784573128798 p{margin:0;}#mermaid-1784573128798 .label{font-family:"trebuchet ms",verdana,arial,sans-serif;color:#333;}#mermaid-1784573128798 .cluste